        {
            "__type__": "Note",
            "fields": [
                "When transforming to state space from diffeqs, how many phase variables \\((x_1 = x, x_2 = \\dot{x}...)\\) do you need?",
                "As many as the number order diffeq, times the number of equations. (second order diffeq&nbsp;\\(\\implies\\)2 variables",
                ""
            ],
            "guid": "D_}eCxyy<>",
            "note_model_uuid": "3a9fd11a-cd92-11f1-9564-7dad70bd0806",
            "tags": []
        },
        {
            "__type__": "Note",
            "fields": [
                "In a typical state space representation of an n-body mechanical system with n equations, how many state variables will there be, and how many rows will have a single one and the rest zeroes in it?",
                "2*n (mechanical creates second-order DEs, second order*n bodies/equations = 2*n).<br>n rows will be all zeroes, except for one 1 (n state variables can just be equated to one of the variables in the DE).",
                ""
            ],
            "guid": "ggx`dLDWn-",
            "note_model_uuid": "3a9fd11a-cd92-11f1-9564-7dad70bd0806",
            "tags": []
        },
        {
            "__type__": "Note",
            "fields": [
                "When transforming from state space to transfer function, what is&nbsp;\\(X(s)\\)?",
                "\\(X(s) = (sI - [A])^{-1} \\ [B] u(s)\\)<br>Where&nbsp;\\(s\\)&nbsp;is a result of the original laplace transform from time domain,&nbsp;\\(I\\)&nbsp;is the identity matrix (e.g.&nbsp;\\(\\left[ \\matrix{1 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 \\\\ 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 0 \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1} \\right]\\)).<br>",
                ""
            ],
            "guid": "f/mQ0HE|aH",
            "note_model_uuid": "3a9fd11a-cd92-11f1-9564-7dad70bd0806",
            "tags": []
        },
        {
            "__type__": "Note",
            "fields": [
                "What is&nbsp;\\(Y(s)\\)&nbsp;when transforming from state space to transfer function?",
                "\\(Y(s) = [C](sI - [A])^{-1} \\ [B]u(s) + [D]u(s)\\)",
                ""
            ],
            "guid": "AayU!D2#^r",
            "note_model_uuid": "3a9fd11a-cd92-11f1-9564-7dad70bd0806",
            "tags": []
        },
        {
            "__type__": "Note",
            "fields": [
                "How to get the inverse of a 2x2&nbsp;matrix",
                "Inverse: matrix that when multiplied by the original yeilds the identity matrix<br>if&nbsp;\\(A = \\left[ \\matrix{a &amp; b \\\\ c &amp; d} \\right]\\)&nbsp;then&nbsp;\\(A^{-1} = \\left (\\frac{1}{ad - bc} \\right) \\left[ \\matrix{d &amp; -b \\\\ -c &amp; a} \\right]\\)<br>Mnemonic: get the inverse of the determinant, multiply by the matrix: exchange the forward diagonal, negate the backward diagonal.",
                ""
            ],
            "guid": "bd*J[IE|{j",
            "note_model_uuid": "3a9fd11a-cd92-11f1-9564-7dad70bd0806",
            "tags": []
        },
        {
            "__type__": "Note",
            "fields": [
                "Original form of a state-space system",
                "\\([\\dot{x}] = [A][x] + [B]u\\)<br>\\(y = [C][x] + [D]u\\)",
                ""
            ],
            "guid": "jElJnD7GoV",
